Based on the [linked esbuild issue](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4436), you can workaround this in Vite this way:

```ts
// vite.config.js

export default {
  esbuild: {
    supported: {
      destructuring: true
    }
  }
}
```

Maybe we can backport this for `@vitejs/plugin-legacy` v7 since this happens on its default setup. Not sure if there's any other syntax that esbuild struggles with for the default range that would've set a precedence though, because I think users should set it explicitly to acknowledge that it may actually not work well in the specified older browsers.

