Yeah, this is a behavior change that is expected. If the value of the import is not used, Vite can (and ideally should) remove the imported file.

Vite 7 and Vite 8 both transforms with `/* #__PURE__ */`, but it seems there's a slightly different behavior in Rollup and Rolldown. Rollup does not seem to remove pure calls before scanning the imports in the file ([REPL](https://rollupjs.org/repl/?version=4.59.0&shareable=eyJleGFtcGxlIjpudWxsLCJtb2R1bGVzIjpbeyJjb2RlIjoiLyogI19fUFVSRV9fICovIE9iamVjdC5hc3NpZ24oe1xuICBzdWI6ICgpID0-IGltcG9ydChcIi4vc3ViLmpzXCIpXG59KSIsImlzRW50cnkiOnRydWUsIm5hbWUiOiJtYWluLmpzIn1dLCJvcHRpb25zIjp7fX0=), the "cannot resolve" error happens). On the other hand, Rolldown seems to remove pure calls ([REPL](https://repl.rolldown.rs/#eNo9jDELwjAQRv/KcS5pKcke0M1ZEdwCIS1RUuwpvatLyH/3XDp88L03vIoP9BWXVMjO/L+EfscBJyXXwyHG6/12jhF6B5dxzpPYxFyeZGogAN5GD6aD4wnK8nmvYgJap1YrAbtATae5jF7WLbc24FfLrySZBdsPk7QpFA==), the "cannot resolve" error does not happen).
The image assets are emitted when the corresponding file is loaded, so it's emitted with Rollup, but not emitted with Rolldown.

Currently, `eager: true` is working, but I don't think that will be guaranteed and may not work in the future. Fundamentally, we need a way to mark the files as an entry and watch them. `build.rolldownOptions.input` cannot watch globs and `import.meta.glob` cannot mark files as an entry.

A workaround I can think of is to write
```js
globalThis.somewhere = import.meta.glob([
    '../images/**',
], { eager: true })
```
and then remove the assignment in `renderChunk`:
```js
function globUsedPlugin() {
    return {
        name: 'glob-used',
        transform: {
            filter: { code: 'import.meta.globUsed' },
            handler(code) {
                return { code: code.replaceAll('import.meta.globUsed', '_bke=import.meta.glob'), map: null }
            }
        },
        renderChunk(code) {
            return { code: code.replaceAll(/_bke\s=\s/g, m => ' '.repeat(m.length)), map: null }
        }
    }
}
```

